      Last updated: September 2026 | 10 min read
    </p>

    <!-- Answer First -->
    <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-6 mb-8">
      <p class="text-theme-primary text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Quick answer:</strong> Mesh count = number of wires per linear inch. Micron rating = particle size the mesh captures. Wire gauge = wire thickness (SWG or AWG). A 100-mesh screen typically filters ~150 micron particles, but the exact rating depends on wire diameter. Use the conversion tables below to specify the correct mesh for your application.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- TOC -->
