    <!-- Section 1: Definitions -->
    <section id="definitions" class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-theme-primary mb-4">1. The Three Ways to Measure Mesh Size</h2>

      <p class="text-theme-secondary mb-6 leading-relaxed">
        Wire mesh is measured using three different systems. Understanding how they relate prevents costly ordering mistakes.
      </p>

      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 mb-6">
        <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Mesh Count</h3>
          <p class="text-theme-secondary text-sm mb-3">
            Number of wires per linear inch (25.4mm). Higher mesh count = smaller openings.
          </p>
          <ul class="text-theme-secondary text-sm space-y-1">
            <li>• Measured by counting wires in 1 inch</li>
            <li> • Standard range: 2–635 mesh</li>
            <li> • Most common in US and Asia</li>
            <li> • Example: 100 mesh = 100 wires/inch</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Micron Rating</h3>
          <p class="text-theme-secondary text-sm mb-3">
            Particle size in micrometers (μm) that the mesh can capture. Direct measure of filtration fineness.
          </p>
          <ul class="text-theme-secondary text-sm space-y-1">
            <li>• 1 micron = 0.001mm</li>
            <li> • Standard range: 1–5000 μm</li>
            <li> • Common in Europe and filtration industry</li>
            <li> • Example: 100 μm captures particles ≥0.1mm</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-6">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary mb-3">Wire Gauge</h3>
          <p class="text-theme-secondary text-sm mb-3">
            Wire thickness. Lower gauge number = thicker wire. Two systems exist: SWG (British) and AWG (American).
          </p>
          <ul class="text-theme-secondary text-sm space-y-1">
            <li>• SWG: Standard Wire Gauge</li>
            <li> • AWG: American Wire Gauge</li>
            <li> • Range: 8 gauge (4mm) to 40 gauge (0.08mm)</li>
            <li> • Always specify in mm to avoid confusion</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary mb-2">Critical Insight</h3>
        <p class="text-theme-secondary">
          <strong>Mesh count alone does not determine filtration rating.</strong> A 100-mesh screen with 0.10mm wire filters ~150 microns. With 0.08mm wire, it filters ~154 microns but has 8% more open area. Always specify <em>both</em> mesh count and wire diameter when ordering.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

