        <p class="text-theme-secondary mb-2">
          <strong>Example: 80 mesh, 0.12mm wire</strong>
        </p>
        <ul class="text-theme-secondary text-sm space-y-1">
          <li>• 80 wires per inch = 80 × 0.12mm = 9.6mm occupied by wire</li>
          <li> • 25.4mm (1 inch) − 9.6mm = 15.8mm open space</li>
          <li> • 15.8mm ÷ 80 openings = 0.1975mm ≈ 198 micron aperture</li>
          <li> • Actual filtration rating ~180 micron (accounts for particle shape)</li>
        </ul>
